# .gcloudignore — controls what `gcloud builds submit` uploads as the build context.
#
# When present, this REPLACES .gitignore-based upload filtering. We need it because
# deployment-api/.gitignore has an UNANCHORED `data/` rule that also matches the
# bundled `ui/src/data/` (capability-manifest-loader.ts etc.) — stripping those app
# source files from the upload made the in-image `tsc` fail with "Cannot find module
# '../data/capability-manifest-loader'" (deploy-shared.sh tier-3 path, 2026-06-14).
# The trigger build escaped this only because it git-clones ui in-container.
#
# Exclude the heavy / generated / secret paths, but keep all app source (incl.
# ui/src/data and the rsync-bundled _unified-api-contracts / _deployment-service /
# codex-data / pm-plans / pm-configs that deploy-shared.sh stages into the context).

.git/
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
node_modules/
*.egg-info/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.qg_last_passed_sha
.qg_content_sentinel

# Local data dir ONLY (anchored to repo root — does NOT match ui/src/data/).
/data/

# Secrets — never upload.
*credentials*.json
service-account*.json
*secret*.json
central-element-323112-*.json
*.json.bak
